    {
      "id": "3724e701-8519-4dfc-bed2-7aa978b96979",
      "phaseId": "8f760a9b-3ce8-4932-8286-67d742397f2e",
      "number": 5,
      "shortName": "context-menu-5",
      "title": "context-menu-5: plugin Contribution::ContextMenu (full design now)",
      "status": "planned",
      "description": "Plugin context-menu contribution. Builds on the ContextMenuRegistry + open_context_menu_for from context-menu-6: the plugin does NOT pass mode/origin (host-internal); it declares context_path + weight + build(target), and the host includes its items when the context is active (keyboard resolve_active_context) or clicked (mouse hit-test). Merge by weight (Dewey Vec<i64>, C2).\n\nLocked design (C1/C2/C3, 2026-07-09):\n- C1 context granularity: dotted context path (e.g. \"sidebar,workspace\" — study the exact dotted form during implementation). The ContextMenuRegistry (context-menu-6) keys providers by ContextPath; the plugin's Contribution::ContextMenu carries its context_path.\n- C2 weight: Vec<i64> Dewey/fractional-index ordering + separators + tie-break. Built-in providers have stable weights; a plugin inserts [1,1,1] between [1,1] and [1,2].\n- C3 native + WASM: full design now (simplifies the contract). Contribution::ContextMenu { context_path: String, weight: Vec<i64>, build: ... } (native closure now; WASM marshalling deferred to plugin-08).\n\nOriginal BACKLOG tasks (context-menu-1..5) superseded by the locked design + the foundation in context-menu-6/7.",
      "notes": "",
